{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9vvk3PQKFxjL3sy2uaJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made the fix and all tests pass. I didn't commit it, because git has no author identity set up here and I didn't want to invent one.\n\n**The problem:** `Hijack()` refused to hijack the connection as soon as anything had been sent, including when only the headers had gone out (after `WriteHeaderNow()` or `Flush()`). Some websocket libraries, such as `github.com/coder/websocket`, send headers first and then hijack, so they failed with `errHijackAlreadyWritten`.\n\n**The fix** (`response_writer.go`):\n- `Hijack()` now rejects only once body bytes have been written. Hijacking is allowed before anything is sent or after headers alone.\n- I added a doc comment explaining this and changed the error message to `\"gin: response body already written\"`.\n\n**Tests** (`response_writer_test.go`): I added two cases to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`: hijacking after `WriteHeaderNow()` and hijacking after `WriteHeader(101)` + `Flush()`. Both now succeed. The existing case where hijacking after `Write()` fails still passes. `go test ./...` and `go vet` pass, and gofmt reports nothing.\n\nTo commit, set `git config user.name` and `git config user.email` and I can commit it with the `fix(response): …` message, or you can commit it yourself. Note that HEAD is detached, so you may want to create a branch first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":439,"cache_read_input_tokens":35259,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":439,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21edd0da-7609-4d3e-937a-41b9a9c5b112","uuid":"69115ca8-676a-442d-956a-f0b7582ee213","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:21:54.122Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9vvjpjaBwbqE3PB27nJ"}
{"duration_api_ms":24645,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"21edd0da-7609-4d3e-937a-41b9a9c5b112","total_cost_usd":0.14189380000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12157,"cache_read_input_tokens":154744,"output_tokens":2506,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":849},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":12157},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":488,"cache_read_input_tokens":35259,"cache_creation_input_tokens":439,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":439,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":2506,"cacheReadInputTokens":154744,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12157,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.14189380000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":849,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I made the fix and all tests pass. I didn't commit it, because git has no author identity set up here and I didn't want to invent one.\n\n**The problem:** `Hijack()` refused to hijack the connection as soon as anything had been sent, including when only the headers had gone out (after `WriteHeaderNow()` or `Flush()`). Some websocket libraries, such as `github.com/coder/websocket`, send headers first and then hijack, so they failed with `errHijackAlreadyWritten`.\n\n**The fix** (`response_writer.go`):\n- `Hijack()` now rejects only once body bytes have been written. Hijacking is allowed before anything is sent or after headers alone.\n- I added a doc comment explaining this and changed the error message to `\"gin: response body already written\"`.\n\n**Tests** (`response_writer_test.go`): I added two cases to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`: hijacking after `WriteHeaderNow()` and hijacking after `WriteHeader(101)` + `Flush()`. Both now succeed. The existing case where hijacking after `Write()` fails still passes. `go test ./...` and `go vet` pass, and gofmt reports nothing.\n\nTo commit, set `git config user.name` and `git config user.email` and I can commit it with the `fix(response): …` message, or you can commit it yourself. Note that HEAD is detached, so you may want to create a branch first.","ttft_ms":4639,"type":"result","duration_ms":55008,"uuid":"62f6a7ea-c835-4bb7-b4c7-4e91fcd268f2","ttft_stream_ms":909,"time_to_request_ms":136,"first_content_frame_ms":910,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
